2026-09-27 20:24:41 | INFO | P04 | CUSTOM OBSERVATIONS:
    Pooled across all three species, flipper length and body mass
    correlate at r = 0.871, which reads as a very strong relationship.

    Recomputing that same correlation inside each species drops it
    substantially in every group. The pooled number is inflated because
    Gentoo penguins are larger than Adelie and Chinstrap on both
    measurements at once, so separating the species removes a size
    difference that the pooled correlation was counting as a
    flipper-to-mass relationship.

    The relationship is real within each species. It is just weaker
    than the headline number suggests, and reporting only the pooled
    figure would overstate how well flipper length predicts body mass
    for any individual penguin.
    
